From 29df2986a48bf717104d3e25a94c4971a4c6a82f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:27:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-81: the split view follows the cursor anywhere in
 an element; Arrange by at the top (0.81.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"所有基礎操作模式能跟WPF一樣方便" (EastSun 20260930):
- WPF's split view: the cursor in the page's HTML beside the designer selects
  the element it is in -- its start tag, its text, a child without an id; in
  <div class="form"> the form (@form). It used to follow only a cursor inside
  a start tag. One pass over the page (htmlblock.openStackAt: the elements open
  at an offset; parentOf is built on it), shared with Shift+F7's finder.
- WPF's "Arrange by" (Name / Category / Source) is at the top of the properties
  list, under the search box -- it was inside the DFM 屬性 section.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 159, smoke 167, panels, real VS Code 148): smoke
(the cursor in spbSave's caption text -> selectId spbSave; in the form div ->
@form), panels (the sort buttons from the header).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
